WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.825
Here's routing on the fixtures.

2
00:00:01.825 --> 00:00:04.400
Day one's twenty-two notices are all new.

3
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.701
Twelve route to a task, nine are
digest only and one is ignored,

4
00:00:08.701 --> 00:00:13.175
so the dry run writes twelve
create payloads and sends nothing.

5
00:00:13.175 --> 00:00:15.108
You can see the routing working:

6
00:00:15.108 --> 00:00:18.824
the security notifications go
to security operations at P2,

7
00:00:18.824 --> 00:00:23.135
the retirements and maintenance to
cloud platform engineering at P3,

8
00:00:23.135 --> 00:00:25.737
and the Azure incident
to the service desk.

9
00:00:25.737 --> 00:00:27.263
Then the important test.

10
00:00:27.263 --> 00:00:31.191
Route the same collection again,
against a copy of the state,

11
00:00:31.191 --> 00:00:35.200
and every notice is unchanged,
so no payload is written at all.

12
00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:39.627
That's what the guide's validate step
asks for: every security advisory and

13
00:00:39.627 --> 00:00:44.563
retirement routes to a task, and a second
run on the same collection writes nothing.

14
00:00:44.563 --> 00:00:48.620
The provider hasn't changed the
notice, so nobody gets a second task.
